  "name": "Arbeiterlied and Kampflied (German workers' fighting song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Political song of the German labour movement, carried by workers' choral societies from the late nineteenth century and sharpened in the Weimar years into the Kampflied, a short marching song for unison singing. Hanns Eisler's settings of Bertolt Brecht and other poets, among them the Solidaritätslied and the Einheitsfrontlied, became its core, and Ernst Busch's recordings of them from the 1930s and later on the East German labels Lied der Zeit and Aurora fixed the performance style.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1930s arbeiterlied and kampflied, protest Song, European branch. choir ensemble, upright piano, trumpet, trombone, snare drum. blanket damped 1925-1945 commercial-major electrical era office. large-diaphragm condenser, tube pre, German tube console. 78rpm shellac.",
